# Alias and legacy-path redirects.
#
# Trailing-slash normalization is intentionally NOT handled here. Cloudflare
# serves the directory-format build output at the trailing-slash URL (200) and
# 308-redirects the non-slash form to it, and astro.config uses
# trailingSlash: 'always' so canonical + sitemap match what is served. The old
# per-path slash-stripping rules (/about/ -> /about, /calculators/*/ -> :splat,
# /guides/*/ -> :splat, etc.) were removed: they contradicted 'always' and were
# already shadowed dead by the directory assets (the slash URL serves 200).

# Host normalization (www -> apex) CANNOT live in this file: Cloudflare Pages
# _redirects explicitly does not support domain-level redirects
# (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects, "Domain-level
# redirects: unsupported" - a host rule here is silently ignored; verified live
# 2026-07-28). Google indexes www separately (uk-mortgage-affordability had 760
# impressions under www despite a correct apex canonical). The fix is a
# zone-level Redirect Rule: Cloudflare dashboard > Rules > Redirect Rules >
# template "Redirect from WWW to Root" (301). Verify with:
#   curl -sI https://www.boring-math.com/   ->  301, Location: https://boring-math.com/

# Privacy: 301 the /privacy alias to the real page. Target MUST be the
# trailing-slash URL: Cloudflare serves the page at /privacy-policy/ (the
# directory asset); a redirect target of /privacy-policy (no file at that exact
# path) does not resolve and 404s, which is why the old rule never fired.
/privacy/                    /privacy-policy/             301
/privacy                     /privacy-policy/             301

# Sitemap redirect (Astro generates sitemap-index.xml)
/sitemap.xml                 /sitemap-index.xml           301
